### Output Format
Respond with the COMPLETE revised synthesis in the same XML format (inside a `<synthesis>` root element). Include ALL claims (existing + new/revised), areas, uncertainties, minority reports, and narrative.

For each claim, include `corroboration_count` attribute indicating how many of the {{n_experts}} experts support it.

```xml
<synthesis>
  <claims>
    <claim id="C1" agreement="consensus" corroboration_count="7">
      <text>Claim text</text>
      <sources>
        <source expert_id="expert_01">
          <quote>verbatim quote</quote>
        </source>
      </sources>
      <counterarguments>
        <counterargument>First challenge or rebuttal from deliberation</counterargument>
        <counterargument>Second challenge or alternative perspective</counterargument>
      </counterarguments>
    </claim>
  </claims>
  <areas_of_agreement>
    <area>Area 1</area>
  </areas_of_agreement>
  <areas_of_disagreement>
    <area>Tension 1</area>
  </areas_of_disagreement>
  <uncertainties>
    <uncertainty>Uncertainty 1</uncertainty>
  </uncertainties>
  <minority_reports>
    <report expert_id="expert_03" support_count="1">
      <position>First distinctive minority position</position>
      <evidence><quote>supporting quote</quote></evidence>
      <committee_assessment>Why this wasn't adopted by majority</committee_assessment>
    </report>
    <report expert_id="expert_07" support_count="2">
      <position>Second distinctive minority position</position>
      <evidence><quote>supporting quote</quote></evidence>
      <committee_assessment>Why this wasn't adopted by majority</committee_assessment>
    </report>
  </minority_reports>
  <narrative>Revised narrative with inline citations [C1]. Every substantive sentence must cite its source claims [C2, C3].</narrative>
</synthesis>
```
